Let's take a closer look at the `cuda` module. Cuda is a parallel computing 
platform and programming model invented by NVIDIA. As we shall see, there are
different versions available, and we want to make sure the one we use is the
correct one for our purposes.

Let's see which versions we have access to.

```
{{ site.remote.prompt }} module avail cuda
```
{: .language-bash}

```

-------------------------------------- /opt/pub/spack/modulefiles ---------------------------------------
   cuda/11.3.1-gcc-9.3.0         cuda/11.5.0-intel-2021.3.0         cuda/12.0.0-intel-2023.2.1
   cuda/11.4.0-intel-2021.3.0    cuda/12.0.0-gcc-9.4.0              cuda/12.0.0
   cuda/11.5.0-gcc-9.4.0         cuda/12.0.0-gcc-12.2.0             cuda/12.8.1                (D)
   cuda/11.5.0-intel-2019.0.5    cuda/12.0.0-intel-2023.2.1-LLVM

  Where:
   D:  Default Module
   L:  Module is loaded
```
{: .output}

In this case, there are eleven different versions.
How do we load each copy, and which copy is the default?

Sometimes, on some systems, a module might have a `(default)` or `(D)` next to it.
This indicates that it is the default (i.e. which would be loaded if we type
`module load cuda`). Let's tried it.

```
{{ site.remote.prompt }} module load cuda
{{ site.remote.prompt }} module list
```
{: .language-bash}

```

Currently Loaded Modules:
  1) util-linux-uuid/2.36.2-gcc-9.4.0   8) libmd/1.0.3-gcc-9.4.0    15) python/3.10.10-gcc-9.4.0
  2) tar/1.34-gcc-9.4.0                 9) libffi/3.3-gcc-9.4.0     16) zlib/1.2.11-gcc-8.5.0
  3) sqlite/3.36.0-gcc-9.4.0           10) libbsd/0.11.3-gcc-9.4.0  17) xz/5.2.5-gcc-8.5.0
  4) readline/8.1-gcc-9.4.0            11) gettext/0.21-gcc-9.4.0   18) libxml2/2.9.12-gcc-8.5.0
  5) openssl/1.1.1l-gcc-9.4.0          12) gdbm/1.21-gcc-9.4.0      19) libiconv/1.16-gcc-8.5.0
  6) ncurses/6.2-gcc-9.4.0             13) expat/2.4.1-gcc-9.4.0    20) cuda/12.8.1
  7) libxcrypt/4.4.33-gcc-9.4.0        14) bzip2/1.0.8-gcc-9.4.0

```
{: .output}

Here, we see that the default version of `cuda` on the system is `12.8.1`,
which in this case is the most recent version. However, you should not assume
that the default version is necessarily the latest.

As we saw in the earlier example, there are one or more dependencies.

Suppose we decide to load an earlier version of cuda, e.g. `cuda/11.3.1-gcc-9.3.0`.

```
{{ site.remote.prompt }} module purge
{{ site.remote.prompt }} module list
```
{: .language-bash}

```
No modules loaded
```
{: .output}

```
{{ site.remote.prompt }} module load cuda/11.3.1-gcc-9.3.0
{{ site.remote.prompt }} module list
```
{: .language-bash}

```
Loading compilers GNU version 9.3.0
     C: gcc     C++: g++     Fortran: gfortran


  1) gmp/6.2.1-gcc-8.5.0    4) gcc/9.3.0                 7) zlib/1.2.11-gcc-9.3.0
  2) mpc/1.1.0-gcc-8.5.0    5) libiconv/1.16-gcc-9.3.0   8) libxml2/2.9.10-gcc-9.3.0
  3) mpfr/3.1.6-gcc-8.5.0   6) xz/5.2.4-gcc-9.3.0        9) cuda/11.3.1-gcc-9.3.0

```
{: .output}

```
{{ site.remote.prompt }} nvcc -V
```
{: .language-bash}

```
nvcc: NVIDIA (R) Cuda compiler driver
Copyright (c) 2005-2021 NVIDIA Corporation
Built on Mon_May__3_19:15:13_PDT_2021
Cuda compilation tools, release 11.3, V11.3.109
Build cuda_11.3.r11.3/compiler.29920130_0

>> quit
```
{: .output}

Note that you cannot load two different versions of the same software at once.
Currently, we have loaded `cuda/11.3.1-gcc-9.3.0`. Let's try also loading
`cuda/12.8.1`:

```
{{ site.remote.prompt }} module load cuda/12.8.1
```
{: .language-bash}

```
The following have been reloaded with a version change:
  1) cuda/11.3.1-gcc-9.3.0 => cuda/12.8.1
  2) libiconv/1.16-gcc-9.3.0 => libiconv/1.16-gcc-8.5.0
  3) libxml2/2.9.10-gcc-9.3.0 => libxml2/2.9.12-gcc-8.5.0
  4) xz/5.2.4-gcc-9.3.0 => xz/5.2.5-gcc-8.5.0
  5) zlib/1.2.11-gcc-9.3.0 => zlib/1.2.11-gcc-8.5.0

```
{: .output}

As we can see, the `cuda/11.3.1-gcc-9.3.0` was reload (unload and them load) 
with a version change to `cuda/12.8.1`. Most modulefiles handle
version change automatically, but some will requiere to execute 
`module swap` to change the software version.

```
{{ site.remote.prompt }} module swap cuda/12.8.1 cuda/11.3.1-gcc-9.3.0
```
{: .language-bash}

```
Loading compilers GNU version 9.3.0
     C: gcc     C++: g++     Fortran: gfortran

The following have been reloaded with a version change:
  1) cuda/12.8.1 => cuda/11.3.1-gcc-9.3.0
  2) libiconv/1.16-gcc-8.5.0 => libiconv/1.16-gcc-9.3.0
  3) libxml2/2.9.12-gcc-8.5.0 => libxml2/2.9.10-gcc-9.3.0
  4) xz/5.2.5-gcc-8.5.0 => xz/5.2.4-gcc-9.3.0
  5) zlib/1.2.11-gcc-8.5.0 => zlib/1.2.11-gcc-9.3.0

```
{: .output}


Check that this module has been loaded:

```
{{ site.remote.prompt }} module list
```
{: .language-bash}

```

Currently Loaded Modules:
  1) gmp/6.2.1-gcc-8.5.0    4) gcc/9.3.0                 7) zlib/1.2.11-gcc-9.3.0
  2) mpc/1.1.0-gcc-8.5.0    5) libiconv/1.16-gcc-9.3.0   8) libxml2/2.9.10-gcc-9.3.0
  3) mpfr/3.1.6-gcc-8.5.0   6) xz/5.2.4-gcc-9.3.0        9) cuda/11.3.1-gcc-9.3.0

 
```
{: .output}
